17592186045417] [17592186341612 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341612 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186340667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341612 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "84898483-2191-5459-b5c9-62b59dd71df8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342134 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341612 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342134 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74035" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342134 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342134 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342134 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "118e9ea0-84b3-5e8f-866f-104da032b6d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342134 #edb/ref 1074 "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ 5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=4 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0.2 & 0.8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0.2 & 0.8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ {x}_{2}+\\,0.2{x}_{3}=0.8 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+0.2(-1)=0.8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\n   \n\nFinally,  substituting ${x}_{2}=1$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(1)=-3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-2.\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=-2$, ${x}_{2}=1$, and ${x}_{3}=-1,$ which means  \n\n$$\n-2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}-{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-2+1-1=-2.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
